WEBVTT

00:00.150 --> 00:10.550
Messier 50 or M 50, also known as NGC 2323 or the Heart-shaped Cluster, is an open cluster of stars in the constellation Monoceros.

00:11.116 --> 00:12.501
It was recorded by G.

00:12.793 --> 00:13.109
D.

00:13.418 --> 00:22.223
Cassini before 1711 and independently discovered by Charles Messier in 1772 while observing Biela's Comet.

00:22.888 --> 00:27.641
It is sometimes described as a 'heart-shaped' figure or a blunt arrowhead.
